<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:id "FTQ-010" ; triage:sprint "c-1" ; triage:severity "important" ; triage:location "crates/bd-cache-sync/tests/cron_hurry.rs:224" ; triage:source "qa-4 /root/c1_flaky4 fenced JSON at95def5f3" ; triage:status "closed" ; triage:record "{\"evidence\": \"cron_hurry.rs:215-225 records timeout(500ms, &mut run), releases the writer, performs management.await, then Err(_) => run.await before testing finished at :236. :403-408 times out the second start after 2s, sets second_stop, then performs second.await. The outer python_lifecycle cleanup at :349-352 is unreachable while this helper remains stuck. RustQA affected-tests log:287-297 reports six successful normal cron_hurry runs, without stalled cleanup coverage.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/tests/cron_hurry.rs\", \"id\": \"FTQ-010\", \"issue\": \"The new production-store lifecycle helper observes shutdown through a 500ms timeout, but its timeout branch awaits the same run without another deadline, after an also-unbounded management await. A shutdown/join regression that persists after writer release therefore hangs instead of reaching finished=false. The rejected-second-start helper similarly follows its 2s timeout with second.await without a deadline; if the wrongly accepted start remains stuck, it never returns to stop/join the first worker and its child. These are precisely the failure paths the lifecycle tests must be able to reject.\", \"line\": 224, \"mechanism\": \"unbounded_wait\", \"recommendation\": \"Give each complete lifecycle fixture an enforceable owned lifetime, preferably a supervised child for scenarios involving synchronous blocking-store work, retaining real worker/task and child cleanup. Bound second-start rejection cleanup and management completion too. Preserve the current causal handshakes and strict elapsed assertions; do not replace retained joins with detached timed-out tasks or increase deadlines.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"ordinary_expiry_joins_the_contended_production_worker_before_writer_release; hurried_expiry_joins_the_contended_production_worker_before_writer_release; zero_timeout_joins_the_contended_worker_without_granting_a_grace_period; rejected_second_start_cannot_reset_the_first_workers_shutdown_deadline\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:qa4Correction "{\"branch\": \"sprint/c-1-runtime-migration\", \"evidence\": \"complete exactly filtered owned fixture, five-second lifetime, timeout/unwind kill/reap, causal stalled cleanup negatives; original inner bounds unchanged\", \"finding\": \"FTQ-010\", \"implementation_state\": \"implemented_pending_independent_QA\", \"logs\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-4/fix-*.log\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-4\", \"receipt\": \"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md#qa4-test-lifetime-correction-ftq-009--ftq-010\", \"review\": \"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6620322598\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:qa5Evidence "{\"finding\": {\"evidence\": \"fixture_child.rs:81-113 reads PID registry once, then kills direct child; common/repo.rs:209-228 performs input=$(cat) before managed_hang PID registration; published sc-cron-0.1.1/src/process.rs:387 uses ProcessGroup::leader(). Source-free probe /tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-5/flaky-pre-registration-probe.py injects a temporary PATH cat delay using the existing built cron_hurry binary. Probe log records test exit 101 at its 5.01s supervisor timeout, with cat PID 39029 and Python stub shell PID 39028, PGID 39028, still alive at 5.5156s after test start. Explicit probe killpg removed both; AFTER_EXPLICIT_PROBE_CLEANUP is [].\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-store/tests/support/fixture_child.rs\", \"id\": \"FTQ-010\", \"issue\": \"The complete fixture deadline kills/reaps its direct test child but can leave a Python process group alive before PID registration. Cleanup snapshots owned-child PID files once, while the Python stub runs input=$(cat) and other commands before writing that registry entry. A stalled command before registration therefore runs in a separate group that is absent from cleanup. Killing the test process removes its runtime and reaper while the Python group survives. The existing stalled/unwind negatives wait until after PID registration and do not cover this path.\", \"line\": 100, \"mechanism\": \"missing_reap\", \"recommendation\": \"Own launched process groups from before they can execute or use a supervisor/subreaper design that covers unregistered launches and prevents spawn during cleanup. Preserve existing strict bounds and actual joins. Add a bounded pre-registration stall negative with process-group disappearance and reap proof; do not rely only on a registry written by the child after startup.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"Python lifecycle fixtures, including rejected_second_start_cannot_reset_the_first_workers_shutdown_deadline\"}, \"probe\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-5/flaky-pre-registration-probe.log\", \"source\": \"QA5 /root/c1_flaky5 exact2111df6f\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:qa5Correction "{\"evidence\": \"kernel session established before actual PythonJob launch; stable stopped census, root kill/wait and post-join session drain; no registry authority; real pre-registration timeout/unwind and exact PATH-cat probe evidence\", \"finding\": \"FTQ-010\", \"implementation_state\": \"implemented_pending_independent_QA\", \"logs\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-5/fix-*\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-5\", \"receipt\": \"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md#qa5-pre-registration-process-ownership-correction-ftq-010\", \"review\": \"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6620709101\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:qa6Evidence "{\"finding\": {\"evidence\": \"session_fixture.rs:142-145 uses Command::output without a deadline; callers session_members, drain and quiesce cannot enforce their own deadlines during that wait. Independent source-free qa-6/flaky-inventory-stall-probe.py pauses only inventory PID58007 (/bin/ps -axo pid=,stat=) at5.0981s while continuing the supervisor. At8.5008s test remains alive beyond five-second fixture lifetime plus250ms/750ms cleanup budgets and seven-second regression watchdog. After explicit SIGCONT of inventory it exits101 at8.6691s; all injected Python PID/group survivors are empty before probe fallback cleanup, and final cleanup is empty. qa-6/flaky-inventory-stall-probe.log records exact evidence.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/tests/common/session_fixture.rs\", \"id\": \"FTQ-010\", \"issue\": \"The PID-registration orphan is repaired, but the new cleanup ownership inventory introduces another unbounded child wait. process_ids executes /bin/ps via synchronous Command::output without a subprocess deadline, inside drain and quiesce nominally bounded loops. If this owned inventory child stalls, the supervisor cannot check its own deadlines, kill/reap the fixture, or fail within its cleanup budget. This is a healthy-kernel user-space subprocess stall, not a mathematical demand to bound kernel syscalls.\", \"line\": 143, \"mechanism\": \"unbounded_wait\", \"recommendation\": \"Give each inventory invocation an owned bounded lifetime with stdout/stderr handling, timeout kill/reap and unwind cleanup, or replace it with an inventory interface that cannot block the supervising thread indefinitely. Count inventory time in the original250ms/750ms cleanup budgets; preserve real PythonJob, strict inner bounds and the repaired pre-registration/session ownership. Add a stalled-inventory negative that fails finitely and cleans both inventory and fixture process trees.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"Python lifecycle SessionFixture cleanup, including rejected_second_start_cannot_reset_the_first_workers_shutdown_deadline\"}, \"inherited_kernel_kill_wait\": \"not_reopened\", \"original_registration_orphan\": \"fixed\", \"probe\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-6/flaky-inventory-stall-probe.log\", \"source\": \"QA6 /root/c1_flaky5 finalfencedJSON exactdc468b9c\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:qa6Correction "{\"evidence\": \"bounded owned inventory; Linux raw SID validation; real Python lifecycle and existing strict budgets retained\", \"finding\": \"FTQ-010\", \"implementation_state\": \"implemented_pending_independent_QA\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-6\", \"receipt\": \"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md#qa6-owned-inventory-and-linux-identity-correction-ftq-010--req-qa-004\", \"review\": \"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6621162334\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:closureEvidence "{\"evidence\": \".cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-1/qa-7/reviewer-handoff.json\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-7\", \"report\": \"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6621585641\", \"scope\": \"Qualified producer-only complete owned fixture cleanup and Linux portability. No C2 finding closure or whole C1 acceptance.\", \"source_commit\": \"5255610a16ef4500f0af508e29a533707a4a3e0a\", \"status\": \"closed\"}" .

